@@ -20,6 +21,21 @@ at startup.
 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.

+## Filtering
+
+The view has a filter bar: free text matched against first and last name, and a
+status selection. Both halves go to the backend as a `CustomerFilter`, which
+`CustomerRepository` applies to the page query and to the count query, so the
+grid keeps holding one page of rows however narrow the filter is. Name matching
+splits the text into terms — every term must appear in one of the two names —
+and ignores case and accents in both directions, so `makinen` finds `Mäkinen`
+and the other way round.
+
+The filter lives in the URL as `?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`, read on entering
+the view and written back with `history.replaceState` as the user edits, so a
+narrowed list can be reloaded or sent to someone else without filling the back
+button with keystrokes.
+
